// A `#test_main` fn that runs every test in its own process, with test::run_here: for a
// `#test{ skip = "why" }` it writes the skip's line and gives test::SKIPPED, 77, without
// running the test. A test that calls test::skip ends that process, with exit code 77,
// after its line and what was written before it: the tests after it don't run, and the
// runner's own code is never reached again.
//# $ ctxc test .
//# exit: 77
//# stdout:
//| one gave 0, skips false ``
//| two gave 77, skips true `not on this machine`
//| written before
//# stderr:
//| ./t.ctx:4: skip: two: not on this machine
//| ./t.ctx:6: skip: three: no game install
